  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the key finding that answers the customer's regression:\n\n**Root cause of the divergence:** DI metadata emission (`Reflect.metadata(\"design:paramtypes\", \u2026)`) is *not* part of either toolchain's core decorator-stage logic \u2014 it's a bolt-on that must be explicitly enabled on both sides, and the two toolchains gate it very differently:\n\n- **Babel**: `@babel/plugin-transform-typescript` (`packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts`) strips TS syntax and has **zero** knowledge of `design:paramtypes`/`Reflect.metadata` \u2014 grep for `emitDecoratorMetadata`/`design:paramtypes` in the whole babel repo returns nothing. `@babel/plugin-proposal-decorators` only decides legacy-vs-stage3 (`index.ts`); the legacy visitor (`transformer-legacy.ts`) implements `applyDecoratedDescriptor`/`initializerWarningHelper` but never emits metadata either. So a Babel+Nest.js pipeline that \"worked\" only worked because the project had bolted on the third-party `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` package (not in this repo) ahead of `proposal-decorators` in the plugins array with `legacy: true`.\n\n- **SWC**: the equivalent logic was ported *natively* into swc's legacy-decorator transform. `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/legacy/metadata.rs` literally credits `leonardfactory/babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` in its doc comments \u2014 it's the same algorithm, reimplemented in Rust. But it only runs when `decorators::Config.legacy == true` **and** `Config.emit_metadata == true` (`decorators/mod.rs`: `if c.legacy { legacy::new(c.emit_metadata) } else { if c.emit_metadata { unimplemented!(...) } ... }`). These map to `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` in `.swcrc`/`crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`. Critically, `swc_ecma_transforms_typescript::Config` (`config.rs`) has **no decorator field at all** \u2014 TS stripping and decorator/metadata emission are fully decoupled passes in swc, wired independently in `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`.\n\n**Why the customer's build silently loses DI metadata:** their `.swcrc` almost certainly sets `legacyDecorator: true` (needed just to parse `@injectable()` the way tsc/Nest expects) but omits `decoratorMetadata: true` \u2014 or sets `legacyDecorator: false`/uses the new stage-3 decorators, which makes `emit_metadata` hit the `unimplemented!()` branch conceptually (metadata is simply never requested/emitted). Classes still construct fine because the class-decorator call (`__decorate`) still fires \u2014 it's only the extra `design:paramtypes` `Reflect.metadata` decorators that go missing, which is exactly why Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` comes back `undefined` at resolution time even though instantiation succeeds. Fix: set both `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator: true` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata: true` in `.swcrc`, matching the Babel-era `legacy: true` decorators option plus the (previously separate) `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` plugin.",
